# fix: List<T>::make disambiguation regression from explicit type-args (owner vs callee) + arity guard
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The first cut of explicit call-site type-args stored a SINGLE `type_args` list on the call and guessed
# whether it bound the owner type or the callee function (`callee_is_fn`). That guess REGRESSED the
# generic static factory `List<i64>::make()` / `Map<K,V>::make()`: `List::make` resolves as a function,
# so the guess routed the `<i64>` (which binds the TYPE `List`) down the explicit-function path and
# raised `'make' is not generic` (10 sites: list_test + map_test). The cure is STRUCTURAL — the two
# positions are recorded separately, no guessing:
#   - AST (`parser::Call`): the single `type_args` is split into `owner_type_args` (the `<…>` on the TYPE
#     before `::`, `Type<T>::m`) and `callee_type_args` (the `<…>` on the FUNCTION/METHOD, `foo<T>()`,
#     `Type::m<T>()`). Either/both/neither may be present.
#   - PARSER: `parse_generic_static_call` records the owner `<…>` and now ALSO accepts a second explicit
#     `<…>` on the method (`Map<str,i64>::fold<Acc>()` → callee_type_args); the bare/function form fills
#     `callee_type_args`; the method desugar carries `mc.type_args` into `callee_type_args`.
#   - CHECKER (`type_call`): `owner_type_args` retargets the factory owner (unchanged #254 path);
#     `callee_type_args` bind the callee's own type-params (explicit-fn path). The `callee_is_fn` guess is
#     gone — the decision is now purely which position the parser filled. `retarget_generic_static_callee`
#     and `collect_call_site_args` read `owner_type_args`.
# GENERIC-ARITY GUARD (owner ruling — C# Func/Action-16 generalized to every generic): a shared
# `max_generic_arity()` (16) gates BOTH a DECLARATION (a type/function/method declaring >16 type-params →
# "a generic may declare at most 16 type parameters", checked in the module-diags pass over items + their
# methods) and a CALL-SITE (>16 explicit type-args in either position → "at most 16 explicit type
# arguments", in `type_call`).
# Acceptance matrix (all build+run exit 0 except the one PRE-EXISTING wall): a non-generic type's static
# methods `Plain::f0()`, `Plain::f1<T>()` (explicit-only), `Plain::f2(x)` (inferred), `Plain::f2<T>(x)`
# (explicit); the generic-type factory `Lst<i64>::make()`; plus the free-fn / instance-method / return-only
# forms. The generic-TYPE + generic-METHOD combination (`Gen<T>::m<U>()`) is a PRE-EXISTING monomorph
# limitation — the #254 instance-method stamp erases method-level type-params (emits `tk_t_U`); it fails
# identically on the pre-feature compiler and is out of scope here.
# Proven by examples/probes/explicit_type_args. Additive over the corpus; the only checker error `teko
# test` still surfaces (checker_test.tkt:1275, an unrelated `list::push`/Variant test) is PRE-EXISTING
# (identical on the pre-feature compiler) and does not affect `build .` or the fixpoint.
